<%#
  The search affordance in the global header.

  It is a plain link to the reference, which is where the site's search lives today.
  Where the page already carries the sidebar's search field, a compiler upgrades the
  link into a button that focuses that field instead of navigating — so the pill never
  promises something the page cannot do.

  The key it advertises is `/`, the shortcut that actually works. When the Search
  station lands its own search, this same element becomes its trigger.
%>
<a class="search-pill" href="/api" aria-label="Search the documentation">
  <i class="fa fa-search search-pill--icon"></i>
  <span class="search-pill--label">Search docs…</span>
  <kbd class="search-pill--key">/</kbd>
</a>
